{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415364-quintessence-and-concentration-camps","id":1415364,"title":"Quintessence and Concentration Camps","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-24T21:42:07-07:00","id":1415364,"title":"Quintessence and Concentration Camps","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> I've been toying with the idea of using a nazi antagonist in my 1940s Mage chronicle. Basically, that nazi is trying to set a mini-concentration camp to get Quintessence off inmates. I remember I read somewhere that a Euthanatoi chantry was getting Quintessence from Dachau, and ITX has a prison for Mages in MECHA (I think), where they do something similar.<br /> <br /> My question is:<br /> <br /> What process do they use to get that Quintessence exactly?<br /> Mechanically, why is it significant those people are in a concentration camp to get Quintessence from them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T01:37:01-07:00","id":1415373,"title":"","content":"Nephandus get quintessence in weird and often horrible ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T02:48:36-07:00","id":1415378,"title":"","content":"(So this is going to be dark, but we knew that going into this thread.)<br /> <br /> <br /> A quick check on <i>M20: How Do You Do That?</i> says that Energy Vampirism - whereby a Mage extracts Quintessence from a living pattern - can be done with either Prime 3 (on a &quot;willing&quot; subject) or Prime 5 (unwilling). &quot;Willing&quot; is in quotation because the target doesn't need to understand what's going on to allow it to happen. Usually, a Mage disguises the act of feeding on Quintessence through some sort of intimate act (sexuality, sensuality, etc), or (in the case of a Primal Utility Mage, getting employees to &quot;give it their all&quot;). HDYDT also says an evil Mage could &quot;rape the energy&quot; (Brucato's words, not mine) out of a person with Prime 3, if they didn't want to be subtle about it.<br /> <br /> That bit about the Primal Utility reinforces the idea that the exact form the extraction process takes is flexible, as all Magickal Effects are. A Mage working at a concentration camp could probably create a steady stream of stolen Quintessence via forced labor or torture. It can be presumed that Nephandi and other evil Mages did this excessively during the Holocaust, and during other times and places where internment and forced labor were employed on a large scale. (Khmer Rouge, North Korea, American slavery, any prison, the present internment of Uighurs in China or Latino immigrants in America, etc). Heck, one could consider that the Prison Industrial Complex was built - at least in the WoD - in part so Syndicate Mages could &quot;mine&quot; Quintessence on an industrial scale.<br /> <br /> You know, more so than they already do as a normal part of Capitalism.<br /> <br /> Indeed, this brings us to the next point: on a large enough scale, you could &quot;automate&quot; the process of exploiting internment for cheap Quint by making such places into Nodes. For Syndicate people, these are Primal Ventures. But it's not a large stretch to assume that Mages of a sinister bent would develop ways to turn a concentration camp into a &quot;Primal Venture&quot; in a similar fashion, just with authoritarian violence as an incentive structure rather than the prospect of meager payment.<br /> <br /> On another note, concentration camps leave open a more direct method for acquiring Quintessence. With Prime 5, the Mage can annihilate an organism utterly, pocketing all the Quint for themselves. Usually this takes the form of some kind of disintegration, but HDYDT states that any suitably significant destruction could be used to make it Coincidental.<br /> <br /> Like, for instance, burning a person alive in an oven.<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously, we must always be careful to not attribute to evil wizards what was principally the fault of normal humans doing evil things. But it would be oddly fitting that evil Mages would push for the adoption of the most extreme practices in concentration camps - likely already being employed in some capacity - in order to profit personally from the death and suffering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T02:49:59-07:00","id":1415379,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine they could use the concentration camp as a focus for using Prime 5 to make an awful node, or maybe utilize a wellspring of quintessence generated by the general mood of the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T05:12:51-07:00","id":1419767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415364-quintessence-and-concentration-camps#post1415364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi.<br /> <br /> I've been toying with the idea of using a nazi antagonist in my 1940s Mage chronicle. Basically, that nazi is trying to set a mini-concentration camp to get Quintessence off inmates. I remember I read somewhere that a Euthanatoi chantry was getting Quintessence from Dachau, and ITX has a prison for Mages in MECHA (I think), where they do something similar.<br /> <br /> My question is:<br /> <br /> What process do they use to get that Quintessence exactly?<br /> Mechanically, why is it significant those people are in a concentration camp to get Quintessence from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is a reason to do this and some logic for why it works. If you were trying to use a Prime effect to get quint from two or more different patterns, it would take one casting for each. If you were spending quint to lower the difficulty, that defeats the purpose. People who are free to live their lives will have different resonance. At a cafe, one person is there to get some work done and another is there to be social. Using a single effect to extract from both people might not work because of the differing resonance. <br /> <br /> The more you change their circumstances and control their environment to impose a state on them, the closer people's resonance with resemble each other. Misery is the default condition for humanity. So, even though it is possible to extract quint consensually in a place of great joy, that requires a lot to make every person joyful. In a concentration camp, you are sure that after a short time, everyone's resonance is going to reflect the misery imposed. One effect to get the quint from everyone. <br /> <br /> As a person is starved and overworked, they lose any semblance of individuality. Their body doesn't have the nutrients to keep the brain at full functionality. Their dreams related to being somewhere else fade and their mind accepts this as the ordeal they must endure until merciful death. Reducing them to this state could make harvesting what remains of their pattern coincidental, whereas doing this to someone who is vibrantly alive would not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415364-quintessence-and-concentration-camps?p=1415378#post1415378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, one could consider that the Prison Industrial Complex was built - at least in the WoD - in part so Syndicate Mages could &quot;mine&quot; Quintessence on an industrial scale.<br /> <br /> You know, more so than they already do as a normal part of Capitalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>A means to expand such an operation efficiently is to have the prisoners doing something that facilitates the import of more victims. Let's say a military-industrial corporation makes surveillance cameras for police agencies to install in high crime cities, but also sells some consumer good. Have the prisoners sawder the parts for the good together. The company buys from the prison and sells the state cameras made in a secure place elsewhere. The cameras installed in high crime neighborhoods are used to nab desperate people doing property crime and cart them off to prison.<br /> <br /> In 1940, the Virtual Adepts were still part of the Technocracy. There is a subgroup called Reality Coders. Their project, Reality 2.0 seeks to reshape the physical reality in which we live. If people stand in the way of that vision, an Adept suffering high Clarity might think it best to move the obstructing population out of the way and extract the quint and labor from them to build the imagined utopia.<br /> <br /> A plot that doesn't require a lot of technology - a lumber camp. Rich men prey on a village with some degree of poverty. They hire young men to cut down trees, some miles from the village. This separates them from the women of marrying age. The rich men turn the most attractive women to prostitution, inviting tourism tied to this trade. After a while, they can even raise the wages of the woodcutters who have no marriage prospects, recouping money spent through brothel revenues. Use the lumber to build a prison camp for anyone who tries to challenge the new order. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}